{% extends 'base.jinja' %}{% block content %}
<section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PREDICTION PLAYGROUND</p><h1>You have a tell.<br><em>Can a bot find it?</em></h1><p class="lede">Rock. Paper. Scissors. Two readable opponents. A private record of what happens when you change your habits.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="{{ url_for('game.dashboard') if current_user.is_authenticated else url_for('auth.register') }}">{{ 'Go to your dashboard' if current_user.is_authenticated else 'Make your first move' }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="{{ url_for('auth.login') }}">Already played? Sign in</a></div><p class="small">One round = one saved result. No real AI, subscription or personal data needed.</p></div><div class="poster" aria-label="Rock, paper and scissors: three moves, endless rematches"><span>ROCK</span><span>PAPER</span><span>SCISSORS</span><div class="poster-foot">HUMAN INSTINCT × SIMPLE RULES</div></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="opponents"><p class="eyebrow">KNOW YOUR OPPONENT</p><h2 id="opponents">Two ways to test your instincts.</h2><div class="cards"><article class="card"><span class="badge">01 / CLOCKWORK</span><h3>Find the rhythm.</h3><p>Cycles rock → paper → scissors, based on how many rounds you have finished. Predictable is the point.</p></article><article class="card accent"><span class="badge">02 / HABIT READER</span><h3>Break your pattern.</h3><p>Counters your most frequent earlier move. It opens with rock. A simple counting rule—not a trained AI model.</p></article></div></section>
{% endblock %}
